  "description": "Binary tree patterns for coding interviews: recursive, iterative and Morris traversals, BFS levels and views, bottom-up returns (height, diameter, max path sum), root-to-leaf paths, build and serialize, and BST basics, with templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Pattern primer</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Trees</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Asked by Meta, Amazon, Microsoft, Google, Uber, Walmart</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Binary Trees</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Five moves cover almost every tree question: walk it (pre/in/post order, recursive, with a stack, or with Morris threads), sweep it level by level with a queue, return a value bottom-up while updating a global answer, carry state top-down along a root-to-leaf path, and rebuild it from a traversal. Add the BST \"interval\" rule and you can read most tree problems in under a minute.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-bst\">Binary search trees</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-tree-lca-views\">Trees: LCA, views, distance-K and serialization</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
